## 🔧 Hardware
| Part | What it does |
|------|--------------|
| Arduino Uno | The brain of the robot |
| L298N motor driver + DC motors | Drives the wheels |
| HC-SR04 ultrasonic sensor + SG90 servo | Detects obstacles and scans left and right |
| TFT display | Shows the animated face |
| DFPlayer Mini + microSD + speaker | Plays sounds |
| Chassis, battery packs, power switch | Body and power |

## 🧠 How it works
1. The ultrasonic sensor measures the distance to whatever is in front of Nexa.
2. If the path is clear, the motors drive forward.
3. If something is too close, Nexa stops, the servo turns the sensor to look around, and Nexa turns toward the side with more space.
4. While this happens, the TFT shows the face and the DFPlayer plays sounds.

