## 🔌 Power setup
Nexa uses two separate power sources. The motors share a battery with everything else at first, and electrical noise from them made the screen flicker and go white. We fixed it by powering the Arduino, display and audio from a separate 9V battery, and the motors from the main battery pack. All the grounds are still connected together.

## 🧗 Challenges and what we learned
- **Screen flicker:** motor noise on a shared battery caused it. A separate battery for the electronics fixed it.
- **Merging working parts:** the obstacle-avoidance code and the face animation each worked alone. Combining them took careful testing. **[EDIT: add what went wrong and how you solved it]**
- **Wiring many modules:** pin conflicts and loose connections taught us to test one part at a time.

